---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, SOCIALS } from '../site.config';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';

const schema = [{ '@type': 'ProfilePage', mainEntity: { '@id': new URL('/#person', Astro.site).href }, url: new URL('/about/', Astro.site).href }];
---

<Base title="About" description="About Kritikesh Rajpurohit: geology and geography graduate learning applied AI." type="profile" {schema}>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <img class="photo" src="/images/kritikesh.jpg" alt="Kritikesh Rajpurohit" width="160" height="160" />
    <h1>About me</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      I'm Kritikesh Rajpurohit, from {SITE.location}. I studied the Earth, I teach what I learn,
      and I'm now building a career in applied AI.
    </p>
    <ul class="what">
      <li>I build with data and AI.</li>
      <li>I map the Earth in QGIS.</li>
      <li>I explain ideas from the basics up.</li>
      <li>I stay curious, without end.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="motto">{SITE.motto}</p>

    <aside class="facts card">
      <h2>Quick facts</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>Name</dt><dd>{SITE.name}</dd>
        <dt>Based in</dt><dd>{SITE.location}</dd>
        <dt>Studying</dt><dd>Applied AI and Agentic AI (EPGP), IIIT Bangalore, 2026 to 2027</dd>
        <dt>Degrees</dt><dd>M.Sc. Geography (IGNOU); B.Sc. (Hons.) Geology (Hansraj College, University of Delhi)</dd>
        <dt>Works with</dt><dd>Python, pandas, QGIS, research and teaching</dd>
        <dt>Writes as</dt><dd>{SITE.blogBrand} (two o's on purpose)</dd>
      </dl>
    </aside>

    <h2>What I'm doing now</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Executive Post Graduate Programme in Applied AI and Agentic AI, IIIT Bangalore (online with upGrad), July 2026 to March 2027.</li>
      <li>Building portfolio projects in data analysis and AI. The first, an analysis of New York taxi demand, is in my <a href="/portfolio/">portfolio</a>.</li>
      <li>Writing a research paper on water poverty in the Bhil tribal region of Banswara, Rajasthan, which includes interviews with residents.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Education</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Programme</th><th>Where</th><th>Years</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>EPGP, Applied AI and Agentic AI</td><td>IIIT Bangalore (via upGrad)</td><td>2026 to 2027</td></tr>
        <tr><td>M.Sc. Geography</td><td>IGNOU</td><td>2023 to 2026</td></tr>
        <tr><td>B.Sc. (Hons.) Geology</td><td>Hansraj College, University of Delhi</td><td>2018 to 2021</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>My M.Sc. dissertation was <em>Tribal Poverty in Southern Rajasthan: A Case Study on Bhil Tribes</em>.</p>

    <h2>Skills, honestly rated</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Working:</strong> QGIS mapping (georeferencing; maps of India and Rajasthan down to village level; watershed, river and peak maps), research and field questionnaires, prompt and AI workflow design.</li>
      <li><strong>Basic:</strong> Python (NumPy, pandas, Matplotlib), SQL, Excel, satellite and terrain data (Landsat, Sentinel, DEM, NDVI).</li>
      <li><strong>Languages:</strong> English and Hindi.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Teaching and exam preparation</h2>
    <p>
      Since 2018 I have prepared for the UPSC and RAS civil services exams alongside my degrees, and I qualified
      UGC-NET Geography for PhD admission. Over the same years I have tutored students for competitive exams.
      I teach from the prerequisites up: fill in the background first, then climb step by step. That method is
      what this site's blog, {SITE.blogBrand}, is built on.
    </p>

    <h2>Outside work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Ideas:</strong> philosophy and psychology, and how they link with mathematics, physics, chemistry and biology. I read across genres, especially self-help.</li>
      <li><strong>Stories and screen:</strong> story writing, film-making, sketching and painting; films of every genre.</li>
      <li><strong>Practice:</strong> Vedic chanting, flute and Rajasthani safa tying.</li>
      <li><strong>Hands-on:</strong> badminton, gardening and cooking.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Find and verify me</h2>
    <p>These are my only official profiles. Each one links back to this site, so you can confirm they are really me.</p>
    <p>{SOCIALS.map((s) => <a class="chip" href={s.href} rel="me noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">{s.label} ✓</a>)}</p>
    {SITE.resumePdf && <p><a class="btn" href={SITE.resumePdf}>Download my resume (PDF)</a></p>}
    <p><a href="/contact/">Get in touch →</a></p>
    <CtaBand />
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .what { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 1rem 0 0.4rem; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem 1.2rem; font-family: var(--font-serif); color: var(--ink); }
  .what li::before { content: "·"; margin-right: 0.45rem; color: var(--accent); }
  .motto { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-style: italic; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .lead { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .facts { margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  .facts h2 { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .facts dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 0.35rem 1rem; margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .facts dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .facts dd { margin: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .facts dl { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .facts dd { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; } }
  .photo { width: 160px; height: 160px; border-radius: 50%; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
</style>
